From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] compositor: retry a single top overlay before full composition

Recovered source for the installed KWin 6.7.4-2+t531overlay1 package.
Preserved by the 2026-11-06 repository audit; this does not establish an
isolated performance benefit. The installed library matches the retained
package byte for byte (see docs/WORKTREE-AUDIT-20261106.md).

A DRM device can expose more individually usable planes than its mixer or
shared line buffer can support at once. On MSM8226 there are three source
pipes but only two configured mixer stages and seven 4 KiB SMP blocks.
Two 1280-wide 32-bit sources need six blocks; a third needs nine.

If the ideal layout fails, try its topmost eligible surface above the
composited remainder before discarding all non-cursor overlays. Reuse the
existing preparation and atomic test paths and retain the normal fallback
on failure. Do not lift a surface past a cursor or composited scene.

This is an active bounded fallback, not a validated performance fix.
It does not handle scene enumeration that already fell back to scene-only,
change the driver overlay allowlist, or fix SMP transition allocation.

---
diff --git a/src/compositor.cpp b/src/compositor.cpp
--- a/src/compositor.cpp
+++ b/src/compositor.cpp
@@ -774,6 +774,23 @@
     auto [layers, result] = setupLayers(primaryView, logicalOutput, output, allowedOutputLayers, *idealLayerAssignments,
                                         frame, SetupType::Ideal, toUpdate);
 
+    // Some KMS devices expose more planes than can be used simultaneously.
+    // Before dropping all overlay candidates, try the topmost surface alone
+    // above a composited scene. Keep the existing cursor/effect ordering:
+    // a cursor or the scene at the top makes this reduced layout unsuitable.
+    if (!result && overlaysAllowed && layerCandidates.size() > 2
+        && qobject_cast<SurfaceItem *>(layerCandidates.front())) {
+        const QList<Item *> reducedCandidates{layerCandidates.front(), scene->containerItem()};
+        if (auto reducedAssignments = assignLayers(primaryView, reducedCandidates, allowedOutputLayers)) {
+            idealLayerAssignments = std::move(reducedAssignments);
+            std::tie(layers, result) = setupLayers(primaryView, logicalOutput, output, allowedOutputLayers,
+                                                  *idealLayerAssignments, frame, SetupType::Ideal, toUpdate);
+            if (result) {
+                qCDebug(KWIN_CORE) << "Using one overlay after full layer assignment failed";
+            }
+        }
+    }
+
     // test and downgrade the configuration until the test is successful
     if (!result) {
         // first, fall back to composited primary + hardware cursor, if that's not already done
